  "findings": [
    "DryRun and Preview both dispatch apply --preview; Hyprland implementation calls pushEval(liveLua) before returning its report, so file-free preview is not pure discovery",
    "Hyprland apply writes settings.lua/settings_window.lua/rebinds.lua in live config and user_edits plus greeter numlock state",
    "outputs calls PATH-resolved ryoku-monitor; scratchpad calls the home-config ryoku-workspace helper; those exact helper sources are not current Source3 selected entries",
    "shared provider detection accepts RYOKU_WM and client constructs ryoku-wm-<name>; process-group cancellation is lifecycle control rather than per-operation authorization",
    "reclaim planning has DNF/XBPS/Pacman adapters, no Zypper; queries/plans require #27 and actual package transactions #28/#29; preserve full switching capability"
